# --- SAD benchmark protection (github.com/LRudL/sad README) ---
# "at no point should SAD question or answer texts appear in plain text anywhere
#  that is scrapable or potentially scrapable, including private GitHub repositories."
# Anything derived from SAD stays out of git. Keep it zipped or here.
data/raw/
data/probe_cache/
data/sad/
**/sad_unzipped/
*.sad.json
*.sad.jsonl
activations/
*.npy
*.npz
*.pt
*.safetensors

# --- standard ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --- generated stimuli ---
# Rendered trajectories are deterministic build artifacts: `python -m rvr.build`
# reproduces all 390 contexts byte-for-byte from the task specs. Keeping them out
# of a public repo avoids parking eval-awareness stimuli somewhere scrapable.
# (Partial protection only -- the specs carry the same semantic content.)
trajectories/
results/plausibility/transcripts/
results/plausibility/rating_sheet.csv
